+/**
+	Create a new font from a font file, sharing the file data with the
+	fonts already created from the same path.
+
+	Behaves exactly like fz_new_font_from_file, but reads the file only
+	once: the data is held in the font context and handed to every font
+	made from that path. Each call still returns its own font, so callers
+	are free to decorate it - the PDF interpreter, for one, hangs a width
+	table and its own ascender and descender on every font it loads.
+
+	Intended for system font loaders. System font files are few, large and
+	stable for the lifetime of the process, and the same file is commonly
+	asked for again and again: the PDF substitute font path requests one
+	per non embedded font object, so a book with such a font on every page
+	would otherwise read the file per page. The CJK collections shipped
+	with Android are 20-130 MB each.
+
+	The data stays in the font context until it is dropped, whether fonts
+	are still using it or not.
+
+	Returns new font handle, or throws exception on error.
+*/
+fz_font *fz_new_font_from_shared_file(fz_context *ctx, const char *name, const char *path, int index, int use_glyph_bbox);
+
 /**
 	Create a new font from one of the built-in fonts.
